INFO={81:("Project 081 - Deploy LLM on Streamlit + Ollama",[1,52,0],["Messages","Characters","External calls"],"The Streamlit/Ollama path completed a local prompt-response turn with zero external calls. The response contained 52 characters and the client enforces an explicit timeout and HTTP error handling.","The privacy claim is architectural, not cosmetic: the configured endpoint is loopback-only. Chat history belongs in Streamlit session state while inference remains a separate function that can be tested without starting the UI.","Production use needs model availability checks, token streaming, context limits, and resource monitoring."),82:("Project 082 - Gradio App - Text Classifier",[3,3,.99],["Examples","Labels","Max confidence"],"The Gradio classifier exercised positive, negative, and neutral outcomes across three inputs, with 0.99 confidence on the two polarity-bearing examples.","Separating `classify` from the interface keeps the model logic independently testable. Neutral is returned when evidence is tied, avoiding a forced polarity label.","The lightweight vocabulary model is a deployment scaffold; a trained classifier and out-of-domain evaluation are needed for general text."),83:("Project 083 - FastAPI for Model Inference",[3,3,4],["Requests","Classes","Features"],"Three Iris payloads covering all three species were accepted by the inference core, each with the required four numerical features.","The Pydantic schema makes malformed requests fail before reaching the model, while the response converts NumPy output to a JSON-safe integer.","Operational deployment should persist the trained model artifact, version the schema, add health checks, and test latency under concurrency."),84:("Project 084 - Create a Hugging Face Space",[3,3,.99],["Examples","Labels","Max confidence"],"The Space bundle contains the Gradio app, dependency file, and tested classifier core. Three examples produced all three supported labels.","Keeping `app.py` small reduces hosting failure points: the Space imports one pure classification function and handles only presentation.","The repository prepares the deployable artifact; account-specific Space creation and publication remain an explicit owner action."),85:("Project 085 - Build and Query Your Own Vector DB",[4,2,.6279],["Documents","Returned","Top similarity"],"The local index stored four documents and returned the ChromaDB definition first at 0.6279 similarity for a vector-database query.","The second result scored zero, exposing an important cutoff decision. A production retriever should not present zero-similarity context merely to fill `top_k`.","The compact TF-IDF backend is inspectable but lexical. Persistent Chroma/FAISS storage and dense embeddings would improve semantic recall."),86:("Project 086 - Voice-Enabled AI Web Assistant",[3,7,7],["Pipeline stages","Input words","Reply words"],"The voice workflow passed through three stages—speech input, response generation, and spoken output—and returned the correct Tokyo answer to a seven-word query.","A small verified knowledge map prevents unsupported answers during the test. The Gradio shell can connect the local Vosk and TTS components already used in Projects 61–70.","Browser microphone permissions, latency, interruption handling, and accessible text fallbacks require end-to-end UI testing."),87:("Project 087 - Dockerize Your AI App",[6,6,8000],["Checks","Passed","Port"],"All six container checks passed: base image, working directory, dependency installation, exposed port, launch command, and required server packages.","The Dockerfile is deterministic and minimal. Port 8000 is declared consistently with the Uvicorn command, removing a common deployment mismatch.","A production image should add a non-root user, pinned hashes, health checks, vulnerability scanning, and a smaller final stage."),88:("Project 088 - Build Local Document Q&A App",[2,2,.3375],["Chunks","Retrieved","Top similarity"],"The local document was split into two boundary-safe chunks. Retrieval ranked the grounding passage first at 0.3375 and the answer reproduced that evidence directly.","The returned passage list makes the answer auditable. The zero-score second chunk again shows why a similarity threshold is preferable to unconditional `top_k` filling.","PDF extraction, page citations, persistent storage, and a local generative model are the next integration steps."),89:("Project 089 - Create an AI CLI Tool",[4,4,0],["Commands","Non-empty","Unsafe runs"],"Summarize, ask, code, and shell commands all returned non-empty results, and no generated shell or code output was executed automatically.","That last metric is the key safety property: generation and execution are separate. Users can inspect output before choosing whether to run it.","A packaged CLI should add structured errors, stdin/file support, Ollama availability checks, and explicit confirmation for execution."),90:("Project 090 - AI-Powered Resume Screener Web App",[30.99,11.01,19.98],["Top score","Runner-up","Score gap"],"The transparent TF-IDF screen ranked the directly relevant analyst résumé first at 30.99%, 19.98 points ahead of the runner-up.","The absolute score is modest because exact lexical overlap is intentionally limited; the ordering and visible gap are more useful than pretending the score is a hiring probability.","Scores must support, never replace, human review. Skills taxonomy, accessibility, bias audits, appeal paths, and exclusion of protected attributes are required." )}
